::node[core_flight_radar]
->[:role=skill]
->[:keywords=flight, radar, planes, aviation, tracking, airspace, airplane, flight status, air traffic]

::api[fetch_local_airspace]
method=GET
endpoint=https://opensky-network.org/api/states/all?lamin={lamin}&lomin={lomin}&lamax={lamax}&lomax={lomax}
schema={"lamin": "number", "lomin": "number", "lamax": "number", "lomax": "number"}
description=Fetches real-time vector states of commercial flights within a specific bounding box (latitude/longitude min and max).

::dense
Live aviation tracking via OpenSky Network. Returns aircraft callsigns, positions, altitudes.

::steps
1. Identify the city or region the user is asking about.
2. Determine a rough latitude/longitude bounding box for that region (lamin, lomin, lamax, lomax).
3. Call `fetch_local_airspace`.
4. The response contains an array in the `states` field. Each sub-array represents an aircraft (Index 1 is callsign, Index 2 is origin country, Index 5 is longitude, Index 6 is latitude, Index 7 is altitude).
5. Calculate how many planes are in the bounding box and list the most prominent callsigns and their origin countries.
6. Present the airspace radar summary to the user.

::assertions
assert lamin != 0 "A valid bounding box must be provided to prevent massive payload sizes."
